{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nBoth engines must produce the same verdict contract, so the claim gate, `review-plan --status`, `sign-review` and MCP status tools need no change. Today the agentic arm [rebar:nickel-ferric-llama] ends in `plan_review_agentic_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py`), which returns an unsigned INDETERMINATE (`agentic-adapter-pending`) carrying the agent's findings on `coverage.agentic_findings`. A failed agent step degrades through `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py`), which records neither the engine nor a failure class: the interpreter keeps only the step's error string.\n\n## Approach\n\n**Adapter.** New `src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py`, `adapt_findings(...)`, called by `plan_review_agentic_verdict` in place of the interim INDETERMINATE. It builds the verdict with the same two functions the pipeline's terminal ops use:\n- maps each agent finding to a pipeline LLM finding: `finding` = `title` + `description`, `evidence` = `[evidence]`, `suggested_fix`, `criteria` filtered to ids in `registry.by_id()` (may be empty), `severity` kept, `tier: \"AGENTIC\"`, and `decision` from severity alone (ADR 0123; operator decision 2026-11-09): `blocker` → `\"block\"`, `major`/`minor`/`trivial` → `\"advisory\"`, with `priority` 0.7/0.4/0.2 so the advisory sort keeps the agent's severity order;\n- calls `orchestrator.partition_findings(det_blocking, det_advisory, mapped, advisory_cap=orchestrator.DEFAULT_ADVISORY_CAP)` (`orchestrator.py:229`), the same call and cap `plan_review_decide` makes (`decide_ops.py:266`). It mints ids with `mint_finding_id` and applies the existing contentless/duplicate narrowing;\n- calls `orchestrator.finalize_verdict` (`orchestrator.py:333`) with `coaching=[]`, coverage `{det, llm_ran: True, engine: \"agentic\", hierarchy_incomplete(+_detail)}` and the frontier model the agent ran on. Zero blockers → PASS; any → BLOCK; `hierarchy_incomplete` → INDETERMINATE, as for the pipeline.\n\nThe verdict op gains inputs `det_blocking`, `det_advisory`, `det_coverage`, `hierarchy_incomplete`, `hierarchy_incomplete_detail` from the precheck (its input schema `plan_review_agentic_verdict_input.schema.json` and the `agentic_verdict` step in `gates/plan-review.yaml`). `ADAPTER_PENDING_ID` and `coverage.agentic_findings` are removed.\n\n**The real post-dispatch path.** After dispatch `_run_plan_review` (`src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py`) does three things:\n1. It runs `_apply_review_floors` (Pass-3 rising/completion/drift floors, xcheck, fix-unit grouping) only under `engine == \"pipeline\"`. That stays: they judge Pass-2 verification fields the agent does not produce and may make LLM sub-calls, while the agentic engine is one agent call (ADR 0123). An agentic floor BLOCK with 2+ DET blockers gets no fix-unit stamps; verdict and findings match the pipeline's.\n2. `_finalize_signature` signs a non-blocking PASS under either engine, so an agentic PASS earns the same certification. The attestation's `engine` field is the next ticket's job [rebar:foliated-oceangoing-parrot].\n3. `sidecar.emit` records the verdict under both engines.\n\n**Reuse shortcuts stay engine-matched.** `reuse.idempotent_reuse`, `reuse.verdict_reuse` and `orchestrator.drift_refresh` already run only under `engine == \"pipeline\"`. Once agentic runs sign PASS and store BLOCK sidecars, a pipeline run could otherwise replay an agentic BLOCK or reuse/re-sign an agentic PASS. New `reuse.latest_review_engine(ticket_id, repo_root)` returns the latest usable sidecar's `coverage.engine`, or `\"pipeline\"` when absent (every pre-existing sidecar). The 3 guards become `engine == \"pipeline\" and basis == \"pipeline\"`, with `basis` read once (`and` operands add no McCabe branch). A signed PASS's sidecar is emitted right after signing, so it names the attestation's engine; the attestation `engine` field [rebar:foliated-oceangoing-parrot] can replace this read. Under `\"agentic\"` the shortcuts stay off, so every agentic review runs the agent.\n\n**Failed and degraded runs.** Provider error, refusal, timeout, limit exhaustion, truncation and schema-invalid output fail the `agentic_review` step and never reach the adapter. Two edits record what the epic requires:\n- `RunnerAgentStep` (`src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py`) keeps the last exception its runner raised (`last_error`). Under `engine == \"agentic\"`, `produce_plan_review_verdict`'s final degrade passes that exception instead of the error string, so `_degraded_plan_review_verdict` records the failure class (`resolution_class`, `disposition`) through the existing `failure.outcome_of` path whenever the raised error carries an outcome (the runner's provider-failure seam attaches one); an error without one degrades with no class, as today.\n- `_run_plan_review` stamps `coverage.engine = engine` on every non-pipeline verdict (floor, adapted or degraded). Pipeline coverage stays byte-identical.\n\n**Carry-over advisories from change 3354.**\n- Fix the stale `engine_route` comment in `plan-review.yaml`.\n- Add `outputs: plan_review_agentic_findings` to the `plan_review_agentic.md` front matter (documents the contract for overrides).\n- Add a test that pins the verdict `model` to the frontier class.\n- Drop the prose \"dollar amounts\" assertion.\n- The floor-tail and degraded-engine points are covered above.\n\nThe output contract already limits severity to the four values, so the adapter has no unknown-severity branch.\n\n## Scope\n\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic_verdict.py (new)\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/agentic.py\n- src/rebar/llm/plan_review/__init__.py, src/rebar/llm/plan_review/reuse.py\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gate_dispatch.py, src/rebar/llm/workflow/runs.py\n- src/rebar/llm/workflow/gates/plan-review.yaml\n- src/rebar/schemas/plan_review_agentic_verdict_input.schema.json\n- src/rebar/llm/reviewers/plan_review_agentic.md\n- docs/config.md (agentic verdicts now PASS/BLOCK)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py (new), tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py (new)\n- tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic.py, tests/unit/test_plan_review_engine_switch.py (replace the interim INDETERMINATE/`agentic-adapter-pending` assertions)\n\n## Testing\n\n- Worked examples via `review_plan(engine=\"agentic\")` with a FakeRunner: `[blocker, major]` → BLOCK with 1 blocking and 1 advisory, unsigned; `[major, trivial]` → PASS with 2 advisories in that order, signed, and `review-plan --status` reports `certified`; `[]` → PASS. Criteria outside the registry are dropped from a finding.\n- Failure: the runner raising `LLMUnavailableError` carrying an outcome → INDETERMINATE with that `resolution_class` and `coverage.engine == \"agentic\"`, with zero attestations written. A plain `RuntimeError` → INDETERMINATE with no class.\n- Engine-matched reuse: after an agentic BLOCK, a pipeline review of the unchanged plan runs the pipeline (no `verdict_reuse`); after an agentic signed PASS, a pipeline review does not report `idempotent_skip`; after a pipeline BLOCK, a pipeline review still reuses it.\n- Pipeline coverage has no `engine` key, and the pipeline's degrade still passes the error string.\n- Schema parity: a pipeline FakeRunner verdict and an agentic verdict both validate against `plan_review_verdict.schema.json`. Both `sidecar.build_payload` payloads carry schema `plan_review_result_v2` with the same top-level keys, and `sidecar.latest_review_result` reads each back.\n- Model: the agentic verdict's `model` equals the frontier class's resolved id.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] The severity mapping, field mapping, PASS signing, failure class, engine stamp and engine-matched reuse are pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_agentic_verdict.py`.\n- [ ] Both engines' verdicts and sidecars satisfy the same contracts, pinned by `tests/unit/test_plan_review_verdict_schema_parity.py`.\n- [ ] `python scripts/check_complexity_baseline.py --check` reports `new=0 increased=0`, and no `src/rebar` file exceeds 800 lines.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1794446953747383001,"uuid":"80fcd72e-501f-43e2-b2f0-c40c7caad8b9"}